  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Coffee Production and Value Addition for Reliable Market Access and Strengthening Members Income</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maki AMCOS produces and exports mild arabica coffee. Located in Mateleka villae in a hard to reach villages in Mbinga District, the AMCOS has a total of 608members of which 161 are women. More than 1,800 members, local farmers and suppliers are direct beneficiaries of this project. The project will use the USADF grant and technical support to increase members income through production and marketing of high quality mild arabica coffee. Looking into the future, value addition is being considered. This will entail roasting of high quality and aromatic Mbinga mild arabica coffee.</narrative>
  </description>
